-- This library prints a recipe's findings between two copies of its
-- summary. `print_findings(summary, lines)` prints the summary, then each
-- line, then the summary again (just once when there are no lines).
--
--   use("cookbook:findings.shale")
--   print_findings("check_errors (Roc): 12 files; 3 errors", lines)
--
-- The summary is printed twice because Shale stops printing at a script's output budget (64 KiB by
-- default, a few hundred lines), so the first copy survives a long list;
-- and roc-chat's verify checks only the last line. A script whose list
-- can be long raises its budget to 4 MB with this line at its top:
--
--   -- budget: output_bytes=4000000

function print_findings(summary, lines)
  print(summary)
  if #lines == 0 then return nil end
  for line in lines do print(line) end
  print(summary)
  return nil
end
